---
import Layout from "../components/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Privacy — Civic Ledger">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">Privacy</h1>
  <p class="mt-2 max-w-prose text-neutral-700">
    This site is built to collect as little as possible — the design goal is that
    a legal demand could not produce information about you, because it was never
    collected. This is a summary; the full threat model lands with the interactive
    features that could otherwise gather data.
  </p>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">What this site is</h2>
  <ul class="mt-2 max-w-prose list-disc space-y-1 pl-5 text-sm text-neutral-700">
    <li>Static pages, built from a dataset the operator maintains. No account, no login.</li>
    <li>No cookies. No analytics. No third-party fonts, scripts, or CDNs.</li>
    <li>Nothing you do here is sent to any server the operator runs.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 class="mt-8 text-sm font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-neutral-500">What is stored</h2>
  <p class="mt-1 max-w-prose text-sm text-neutral-700">
    There is no per-visitor data of any kind — visiting this site leaves no
    record anywhere. Every fact on a member, vote, or bill page links to the
    original government record it came from, so you can check it yourself.
    The dataset and source code are not currently published in a public
    repository; a legal demand to the operator would produce only what that
    private repository contains, none of it about site visitors.
  </p>

  <p class="mt-8 text-xs text-neutral-500">
    Interactive tools (added later) keep your results only in your own browser,
    with a button to erase them. The full threat model will document every such
    surface before it ships.
  </p>
</Layout>
